            <ArticleTitle>Burn care: a social work perspective.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-106</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The psychosocial problems of people who have been severely burned are many and severe. Written according to the outline followed by the articles in Health and Social Work's November 1981 Supplement on Specialization and Specialty Interests, this article describes the complexities of burn treatment and the key role of the social worker in burn care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
